> Read and modify player XP levels, and set the progress bar by fraction rather than by points.

name XP
slug bookshelf-xp
version 5.0.0
tags runtime
authors Aksiome, Leirof


feature function add_levels > Add levels to players.
  since 2022/04/14 1.18.2
  @executor: player[] > players to add levels to
  input arguments
    levels: int > levels to add, negative to remove
  output state > the experience bar is updated

feature function add_points > Add experience points to players.
  since 2022/04/14 1.18.2
  @executor: player[] > players to add points to
  input arguments
    points: int > points to add, negative to remove
  output state > the experience bar is updated

feature function add_progress > Add progress to the experience bar.
  since 2023/08/31 1.20.1
  @executor: player[] > players to add bar progress to
  input arguments
    progress: float @ -1..1 > fraction of the bar to add, negative to remove
  output state > the experience bar is updated

feature function get_progress > Get the fill progress of the experience bar.
  since 2022/04/14 1.18.2
  @executor: player > player to get the bar progress from
  output storage: float @ 0..1 > fraction of the bar filled

feature function get_remaining_points > Get the number of points missing to reach the next level.
  since 2023/08/31 1.20.1
  @executor: player > player to get the remaining points from
  output storage: int @ 0.. > points still needed to reach the next level

feature function get_required_points > Get the number of points the current level holds.
  since 2023/08/31 1.20.1
  @executor: player > player to get the required points from
  output storage: int @ 0.. > points needed to fill the current level

feature function get_total_points > Get the total number of points a player has, levels included.
  since 2022/04/14 1.18.2
  @executor: player > player to get the total points from
  output storage: int @ 0.. > total number of points, levels included

feature function set_levels > Set the level of players.
  since 2022/04/14 1.18.2
  @executor: player[] > players to set the levels of
  input arguments
    levels: int @ 0.. > level to set
  output state > the experience bar is updated

feature function set_points > Set the experience points of players.
  since 2022/04/14 1.18.2
  @executor: player[] > players to set the points of
  input arguments
    points: int @ 0.. > points to set within the current level
  output state > the experience bar is updated

feature function set_progress > Set the fill progress of the experience bar.
  since 2022/04/14 1.18.2
  @executor: player[] > players to set the bar progress of
  input arguments
    progress: float @ 0..1 > fraction of the bar to fill
  output state > the experience bar is updated

feature function set_total_points > Set the total experience points of players.
  since 2022/04/14 1.18.2
  @executor: player[] > players to set the total points of
  input arguments
    points: int @ 0.. > total number of points to set, levels included
  output state > the experience bar is updated
